{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0671"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge nature/mammals","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/nature__mammals.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",370],["+","One lemur holds an unusual distinction: the blue-eyed black lemur (Eulemur flavifrons) of north-western Madagascar, first described by John Edward Gray in 1867, is the only primate apart from some humans to have consistently blue eyes. "],["=",595]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",352],["+","Ein Lemur hat eine ungewöhnliche Besonderheit: Der Blauaugenmaki (Eulemur flavifrons) aus dem Nordwesten Madagaskars, 1867 von John Edward Gray erstmals beschrieben, ist der einzige Primat, der – von manchen Menschen abgesehen – regelmäßig blaue Augen hat. "],["=",553]]},{"field":"notesEn","old":"","new":"Strictly, Wikipedia calls the blue-eyed black lemur 'one of the only primates other than humans' with consistently blue eyes."},{"field":"notesDe","old":"","new":"Genau genommen nennt Wikipedia den Blauaugenmaki „einen der wenigen Primaten außer dem Menschen“ mit durchweg blauen Augen."}]},
